{
  "feature_instruction": "## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#800020] text-white\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#D4AF37] hover:bg-[#b8942e] text-white font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#D4AF37]\n- Section bg: bg-white (odd sections) / bg-gray-50 (even sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white\n- Body: text-gray-700 leading-relaxed\n\nThis feature provides a comprehensive menu display for Farmaaish Restaurant, allowing customers to browse dishes by category and add them to their cart. It consists of a service (`menuService.ts`) for interacting with the backend menu API, a custom React Query hook (`useMenu.ts`) for data fetching and caching, TypeScript types (`menu.ts`) for menu entities, and several UI components to render the menu.\n\nThe `MenuPage.tsx` serves as the main entry point, orchestrating the display of menu categories and items. It utilizes `useMenu.ts` to fetch all menu categories and items. The categories are rendered using `MenuCategoryTabs.tsx`, which allows users to filter the displayed menu items. The filtered menu items are then passed to `MenuItemsGrid.tsx`, which in turn renders individual `MenuItemCard.tsx` components. Each `MenuItemCard.tsx` displays the dish's name, description, price, and an image, along with an `AddToCartButton` from the `order-flow` feature. The `AddToCartButton` will call `useCart().addItem()` to add the selected menu item to the shopping cart.\n\nAll monetary values (prices) displayed in this feature must be formatted in Indian Rupees (₹) using the `en-IN` locale.\n\n### `menuService.ts`\nThis service is responsible for making API calls to the `menu-management` backend feature. It exports two asynchronous functions:\n1. `getAllMenuItems(): Promise<MenuItemDto[]>`: Fetches all menu items from the `/api/v1/menu/items` endpoint.\n2. `getAllMenuItemCategories(): Promise<MenuItemCategoryDto[]>`: Fetches all menu categories from the `/api/v1/menu/categories` endpoint.\n\nBoth functions use the `apiClient` from `frontend/src/api/client.ts` to perform GET requests and return the parsed JSON response.\n\n### `useMenu.ts`\nThis custom React Query hook provides an interface for components to fetch and manage menu data. It exports the `useMenu()` hook with the following capabilities:\n1. `useMenu()`: Returns an object containing:\n    - `menuItems: MenuItemDto[]`: A list of all menu items.\n    - `categories: MenuItemCategoryDto[]`: A list of all menu categories.\n    - `isLoading: boolean`: A boolean indicating if data is currently being fetched.\n    - `error: Error | null`: Any error that occurred during data fetching.\n\nIt internally uses `react-query`'s `useQuery` to call `menuService.getAllMenuItems()` and `menuService.getAllMenuItemCategories()`, caching the results. The `MenuItemDto` and `MenuItemCategoryDto` types are imported from `frontend/src/types/menu.ts`.\n\n### `menu.ts`\nThis file defines the TypeScript interfaces for `MenuItemDto` and `MenuItemCategoryDto` based on the `menu-management` backend's `MenuItemDto` and `MenuItemCategoryDto` data shapes. These types ensure strong typing throughout the frontend application when dealing with menu data.\n\n### `MenuPage.tsx`\nThis page component displays the full menu of Farmaaish Restaurant. It uses the `Layout` component from `core-ui` for consistent navigation and footer. The page fetches all menu items and categories using `useMenu()`. It manages the currently selected category state. It renders a hero section with a background image, the restaurant name, and a welcoming message. Below the hero, it displays `MenuCategoryTabs` to allow users to filter items by category. The `MenuItemsGrid` component then renders the menu items belonging to the selected category. All prices are formatted in Indian Rupees (₹).\n\n### `MenuCategoryTabs.tsx`\nThis component renders a tabbed interface for menu categories. It receives a list of `MenuItemCategoryDto` and a callback function `onSelectCategory(categoryId: UUID | null)`. When a tab is clicked, it calls `onSelectCategory` with the `id` of the selected category or `null` for "All" categories. The active tab is visually highlighted using Tailwind CSS classes.\n\n### `MenuItemsGrid.tsx`\nThis component displays a grid of `MenuItemCard.tsx` components. It receives a `List<MenuItemDto>` as a prop, representing the menu items to display. It iterates over this list and renders a `MenuItemCard` for each item. The grid layout is responsive, adapting to different screen sizes.\n\n### `MenuItemCard.tsx`\nThis component renders a single menu item card. It receives a `MenuItemDto` as a prop. It displays the item's `imageUrl`, `name`, `description`, and `price`. The price is formatted in Indian Rupees (₹). It includes an `AddToCartButton` component from the `order-flow` feature, passing the `MenuItemDto`'s `id`, `name`, `unitPrice` (which is `price`), and `imageUrl` to it. The `AddToCartButton` will handle adding the item to the cart.",
